WEBVTT

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:26.020
Mom. Dad. I've been made
squad captain for the next mission.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.590
It's a major operation
to rescue friendly forces,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.960
but I will do my very best
not to shame the Werec name.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.370
My only concern is Sara,
who'll be left all alone...

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.440
Ralph-oniichan...

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.110
Sara.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.050
Here...

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.050
I drew this.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.120
It's a picture of you.
Take it with you...

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.850
Thanks. I'll take great care of it.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.450
This is for the picture.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:28.250
Now we both have one.
Now we'll always be together.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.580
And actually, it does this...

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.930
Come here, Sara.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.700
You've improved.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.170
The Box Step is basic!

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.770
I bet you'll be even more
skillful when I return!

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.120
You're going 130 light years away!

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:01.950
You know I'll be long dead
by the time you come back!

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.780
Sara...

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.290
Sara... I have to go now...

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.140
I'll be back.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.640
I'm...

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.820
I'm going to go!

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.930
To where you'll be!

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.920
Sara...

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.370
Only you can accomplish
what you've decided.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:56.700
As long as you believe in that,
there's surely nothing you can't do!

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.140
I'll be back!

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.810
Yes... I absolutely will go!

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.480
To where my brother is!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.430
Prelude to Despair

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.380
Here we go, Sara!

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.990
This is no sweat at all!

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.570
Sara! You seem to be doing
exceptionally well today!

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.940
Just like every other day!

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.410
But please leave some for us, too!

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.740
These ones are mine!

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.810
You're doing a good job
of driving them into a corner!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.590
Got 'em!

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.250
That's not fair!

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.930
Not bad, Cedie!

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:26.760
I'll never beat Ralph Werec
if I always let you outdo me!

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.100
Whatever.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.090
Let's clean up the rest!

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.280
Group B, training exercise complete.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:42.710
Top honors go to Strain 01.
Reasoner Sara Werec.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.550
46 dummy TUMORs downed.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.950
I'd expect no less from a Werec.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.150
Yes.

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:54.360
So the Grabera Spatial Armor
Infantry Research Institute

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.730
can send another of its finest
Reasoners again this semester...

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.840
Good work today!

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.780
Mimic storing completed.
Mercurion circulation starts.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.980
Let's work hard again tomorrow, okay?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.380
Cedie!

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.090
Umm, say, Sara...

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.090
Yeah?

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:26.960
No, uhh, you know, on our
next day off, would you-

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.430
Hey, you two!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.600
What are you standing around for?
The next lecture's about to begin!

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.900
We'll go on ahead!

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.770
Wait! Hold on!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.100
Let's hurry!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.270
It's no use. I can't say it...

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.680
C'mon, Cedie! Hurry!

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:46.670
Right!

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.520
Wait for me, Brother!

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.800
With the discovery of Mercurion,

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.430
mankind gained the means
to approach the speed of light.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.200
The conflicts that occurred with
the resulting territorial expansion

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.870
caused a split within mankind, however.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.710
Many years have passed
since war first broke out

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.380
between us, the Union, and the Deague.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:25.720
We can say that this fighting
itself is now part of human history.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.620
Maintaining the expanded battle lines

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:32.260
requires ceaseless technological
innovation and top-notch manpower;

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:36.730
the first being the Strains,
and the second being you Reasoners.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.600
We are not scientists.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:42.970
As such, we cannot turn the tide
of the war with new technology.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:47.200
There's only one thing we can do:
polish our skills as Reasoners.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.810
Hey, Mary.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.470
What is it, Colin?

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.010
Is there still no progress with those two?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.010
It... would seem not.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.650
Yeesh. Cedie has no drive at all.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:05.260
All Sara thinks about is her brother.
It won't be that easy for him.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.990
Ralph Werec, for example!

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:13.100
He is the finest Reasoner
to have graduated from this academy.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.770
In the recent Alabomeris campaign,
he downed ten Deague warships

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.970
and was the youngest person
ever to receive a Gloire Strain.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:26.210
What we most need now are
first-rate Reasoners like him!

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:31.880
That is how we will achieve
victory in this longstanding war!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.720
Here we go now.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.880
Ahh! Wait up!

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:45.330
You almost got left behind, you know.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.520
S-sorry...

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.370
I can't wait to be like Sara's brother!

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.070
It won't be long now!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:57.340
Only 20 flight hours left
until graduation exercises!

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.140
The sub-light speed exercises, huh...

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:03.180
Yeah. I'll be able to go
to my brother soon...

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:07.020
There you have it. You got it rough,
Cedie, with someone like her.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.220
W-what are you talking about,
Colin?! Sara isn't-

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.320
Huh? What?

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.960
Uhh, nothing...

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.230
It's Higgins...

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:20.220
He let his Mimic get damaged
recently, as I recall...

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:28.900
What do you suppose he's going to do now?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.950
Your Mimic contains cultured
brain cells harvested from you

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.980
while you were still just
in your mother's womb!

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:43.720
In other words, it's like your twin!
If it dies, it's not coming back!

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:47.530
The moment you lose your Mimic,
you are no longer a Reasoner!

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.860
You'll be a useless nobody from then on!

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.860
Listen!

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.300
Take better care of your Mimic
than you would yourself!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.670
We can create replacement limbs,
but not replacement Mimics!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.370
Too slow! I'll see your ass in detention!

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:04.380
Next!

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.810
No dilly-dallying!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.850
Soon we won't have Instructor
Havisham's sage advice anymore...

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:12.180
Though, to be honest, he's a real earful.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.220
I can hear you! I have just
one thing to say to that!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.760
"When things look bad, screw up good!"

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:22.560
Right, Instructor Havisham?

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.220
That's correct!

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:31.770
Well, you guys've been top of
the class for some years now.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:36.440
If you keep goin' as you are,
you could be the next Ralph Werec!

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.540
Especially you, Sara Werec!

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.880
Work hard, if you don't want
your brother to leave you behind!

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.750
Yes, sir!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.450
Guess you never managed
to ask Sara out, huh?

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.020
I just couldn't find the right time...

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:55.490
Yes, her brother is the only
person she talks about...

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:59.330
But once we graduate, we'll all
be assigned to different places!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:02.600
--If you don't do something now...
--Yeah, I know.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.670
Hey. Whatcha talking about?

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.370
Sara! Nothing! Nothing at all!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.340
Sara! The truth is-

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:10.610
Don't say it! Don't say it!

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.410
What? What're you freaking out about?

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.710
Oh, uhh... Well, you see...

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:18.680
C'mon, what is it?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.850
--No, uhh, you see...
--No, uhh, you see...

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.550
Yeesh! What is it?!

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.840
Soon, Brother.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:43.510
Soon I'll be able to go
to the same place you are.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:44.840
Wait for me.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:50.150
Snuck out of the dorms in
the middle of the night again?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.380
Don't blame me if they yell at you!

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:57.820
I don't mind. I'm perfectly fine
with getting yelled at a bit.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:02.160
After all, this is the closest spot
to the sky where my brother is.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.190
Again, with your brother?

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:08.100
You must really like him. I'm jealous...

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:12.770
He's the only brother I have
in this world. It's only natural.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.800
Yeah...

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.340
Hey. Indulge me.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:20.280
Huh?!

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:23.270
I'll see if you've gotten any better!

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:28.040
Please be gentle...

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:39.700
C'mon, Cedie! Not so fast!

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:43.700
I've gotten a little better;
can't you praise me even a bit?

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:47.440
Nope, not yet!
I don't want to pamper you!

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:51.780
I can't help that I'm not as versatile
as a certain someone's brother.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.410
I know that.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.740
--Oww!
--Oh! Sorry!

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.950
How are they doing?

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.920
They're dancing again.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.120
No progress, then...

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.090
Sheesh! He could at least
hold her shoulder!

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:14.060
This must be a case of
"just being close makes me happy."

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:16.730
I don't think it is!

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.080
What could that be?

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.370
Are they doing night-time
exercises or something?

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.370
A Deague attack?! That's absurd!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.640
What would they have to gain by
attacking this far behind lines?!

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.300
This is Grabera, for chrissakes!

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:57.510
Unable to contact Central Command!
All links are down!

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:00.410
No feeds from the geodetic
satellites, either!

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.410
What are the in-orbit forces doing?!

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:05.550
TUMORs are falling into
the urban district, too!

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:06.880
What was that?!

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.790
T-the dormitories!

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:13.660
Aid and evacuate the cadets!
We mustn't let any more die!

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.560
Hobbs-kun! You're in charge!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.000
Yes, sir! Everyone who's
not working, follow me!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.730
--Yes, sir!
--Havisham-kun!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:21.570
--You're...
--Taking a Strain out there!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.620
What... What's happening?!

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:37.640
Sara!

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.410
Cedie! Look up there!

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.760
--TUMORs...
--No way!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.130
How did they slip through
the security net?

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:52.130
Sara! Where are you going?!

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.530
Where do you think?!
I'm taking a Strain out there!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.190
That's crazy! Sara!

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:06.240
Thank goodness!
The Garden's still alright!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.850
You're both all right?!

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:17.290
--What took so long, Sara?!
--Please hurry!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.860
We can't count on the command
tower to give instructions!

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.590
I can't believe such a large
number of TUMORs snuck in!

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:28.130
No doubt someone betrayed us
and brought the Deague here!

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.300
There's no point in discussing it now!

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.500
We gotta manage to survive this somehow!

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.060
Here they come!

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:04.000
Around 5000 total, from the looks of it...

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.340
We're goners if we don't
pull through this...

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:08.510
Sara!

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:12.310
Don't worry! We just need
to do it like in our exercises!

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:15.910
Besides, we can't die in a place like this!

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.250
Let's do it, guys!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.910
--Roger!
--Roger!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.530
What's that?!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.370
A Gloire Strain?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.200
Is it a friendly?!

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:42.270
About time it shows up!
Where was it all this time?!

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.430
No... Something's not right!

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.770
Huh? What do you mean?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:00.120
Y-you can't be serious!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.780
Sara! Stop!

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.160
That's nothing!

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.470
Run!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.570
Sara!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.040
Cedie!

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.940
If I remember right,
an old army lab is that way...

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.800
Is that what they're after?!

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.000
The Reasoner's inside!

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:35.880
Colin...

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.120
Mary...

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.840
Cedie...

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:49.950
That's him!

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.940
There he is!

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.870
Don't move, traitor!

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:18.020
You're a Reasoner, yet you betrayed us
and brought the enemy here!

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:19.760
...And killed everyone!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.220
How dare you...

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:27.800
How dare you kill Colin
and Mary and Cedie!

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.730
You will... You will pay for this!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:52.190
B- Brother?

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:18.750
Brother!

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:32.980
I'm borrowing this!

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.110
Brother!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:45.300
Brother! Why?! Why are you doing this?!

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:03.000
There's still something I can do.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:06.140
It's a different path, but
I can head to where my brother is.

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:08.140
No matter what the circumstances may be.

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:11.470
On the next Soukou no Strain: Encounter

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:13.470
Is this fate?
